// Title: Remote XSL Execution Via Msxsl.EXE
// Sigma ID: 75d0a94e-6252-448d-a7be-d953dff527bb
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel
// Date: 2023-11-09 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1220
// Description: Detects the execution of the "msxsl" binary with an "http" keyword in the command line. This
//   might indicate a potential remote execution of XSL files.
// False positives:
//   - Msxsl is not installed by default and is deprecated, so unlikely on most systems.
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1220/T1220.md
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/OtherMSBinaries/Msxsl/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_msxsl_remote_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\msxsl.exe" and ProcessCommandLine contains "http"
